{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2148-07-16 13:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hello, I'm Dr. Lee, one of the surgical team. You're here because of your rectal prolapse that's been getting worse. Can you tell me more about what’s been happening?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2148-07-16 13:16:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, thank you. It’s been going on for months, but now it happens every time I go to the bathroom. Sometimes even when I walk. It goes back in on its own, but I can’t feel much down there and I leak stool and gas. I wear a pad every day."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2148-07-16 13:17:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. That must be very uncomfortable and concerning. You also mentioned some blood in your bowel movements and left lower abdominal pain?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2148-07-16 13:18:20",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, there’s often a little blood, and I’ve had a dull ache on the left side. And just in the last few days, I’ve gained about 10 pounds. I’m worried that’s my heart again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2148-07-16 13:19:10",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s a good point. You have a history of heart failure, so we’ll monitor your fluid status closely. We’ll check your labs and start you on your usual diuretics to help with that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2148-07-16 13:20:05",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that makes me feel better. What about the surgery? I know we talked about it, but I’m nervous."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2148-07-16 13:21:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re planning a perineal rectosigmoidectomy with levatorplasty. It’s a procedure to repair the prolapse through the rectum, not the abdomen. It’s less invasive and better suited for someone with your medical history."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2148-07-16 13:22:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And I’ll be asleep? I won’t feel anything?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2148-07-16 13:22:40",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, you’ll be under general anesthesia. You’ll be completely asleep. We’ll also give you antibiotics beforehand to prevent infection."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2148-07-16 13:23:20",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. I’ve been on senna and Miralax, but it hasn’t helped much. I still can’t control things."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2148-07-16 13:24:05",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s common with long-standing prolapse and nerve changes. After surgery, we’ll restart your bowel regimen carefully to avoid straining."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2148-07-16 13:25:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. I just want to be able to live normally again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2148-07-17 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Today is your surgery day. You’ve had your bowel prep with magnesium citrate, and we’re all set. Any questions before we head to the OR?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2148-07-17 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No, I trust you. Just please take care of me."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2148-07-17 08:03:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We will. You’re in good hands. See you when you wake up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2148-07-17 15:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, you’re back in your room. The surgery went very well. You had a perineal rectosigmoidectomy, and everything was completed without issues. How are you feeling?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2148-07-17 15:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Tired… a little groggy. My belly feels full, but not painful."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2148-07-17 15:33:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s expected. Your bowels are still waking up after surgery and anesthesia. We call that an ileus. You’ll start with sips of water and advance slowly."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2148-07-17 15:34:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I don’t feel like eating anyway. But I haven’t peed much. Is that normal?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2148-07-17 15:36:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You had low urine output earlier, so we gave you some IV fluids. We’ve now restarted your torsemide and spironolactone. You should start making more urine soon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2148-07-17 15:37:20",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, good. My heart’s been okay, right?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2148-07-17 15:38:10",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, your vitals are stable. No signs of heart failure. We’re watching closely."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2148-07-18 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your labs show your hemoglobin is 9.2, which is a bit low but stable. Platelets are 81, which we expected given your history of autoimmune thrombocytopenia."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2148-07-18 09:01:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that safe? Should I be worried?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2148-07-18 09:02:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "No, it’s within an acceptable range for you. We’re not planning a transfusion. We’ll keep monitoring."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2148-07-18 09:03:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. My belly still feels very bloated."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2148-07-18 09:04:20",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, the abdominal X-ray shows your large bowel is distended. This supports the ileus. But you’re passing gas, which is a good sign. We’ll keep you on clear liquids for now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2148-07-18 09:05:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I wish it would move. I hate feeling like this."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2148-07-18 09:06:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I understand. It will take time. We’re not worried, just being cautious."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2148-07-19 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You passed flatus this morning — that’s great! It means your bowels are starting to wake up. We’re going to advance your diet to clear liquids today."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2148-07-19 10:01:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Really? That’s progress! Can I have broth?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2148-07-19 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, broth, juice, tea — all clear liquids. We’ll see how you tolerate it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2148-07-20 08:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your urine test came back with a small amount of bacteria, less than 10,000 organisms/ml. It’s a mild UTI, so we’re starting you on ciprofloxacin to prevent it from getting worse."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2148-07-20 08:31:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh, I haven’t had any burning or urgency. Is it serious?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2148-07-20 08:32:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not at all. Sometimes infections are silent, especially after surgery. Better to treat it early."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2148-07-20 08:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Makes sense. Thank you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2148-07-21 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing well. You’ve been tolerating liquids, and your abdomen is less distended. We’re going to try a soft diet today."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2148-07-21 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Great! I’m ready for real food. But I still haven’t had a bowel movement."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2148-07-21 09:02:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s okay. It’s only been a few days. We’ve started you on senna to help gently. No straining, remember."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2148-07-21 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I won’t. I’m just anxious about it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2148-07-21 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your body is healing. We’re not in a rush."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2148-07-22 08:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The chest X-ray shows your heart is still moderately enlarged, but no fluid in the lungs. The abdominal X-ray shows improvement in distention."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2148-07-22 08:31:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So my heart’s okay? And my belly’s getting better?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2148-07-22 08:32:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes on both counts. You’re making steady progress."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2148-07-22 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You passed a small bowel movement this afternoon — excellent! That means your ileus is resolving."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2148-07-22 14:01:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "It was small, but I’m so glad. Does this mean I can go home soon?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2148-07-22 14:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Possibly tomorrow. We want to make sure you’re eating well, your pain is controlled with oral meds, and you’re mobile."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2148-07-22 14:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I feel ready. I’ve been walking in the hall every few hours."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2148-07-22 14:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s perfect. Keep it up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2148-07-23 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good news — you’re being discharged today. You’re tolerating a regular diet, passing gas, and your pain is well managed with oral meds."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2148-07-23 09:01:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh, that’s wonderful! What do I need to do at home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2148-07-23 09:02:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll take ciprofloxacin for the UTI, and pain meds as needed. Continue your stool softener and senna to avoid constipation. No heavy lifting for six weeks."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2148-07-23 09:03:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And if I see blood?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2148-07-23 09:04:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "A little dark blood is normal. But if you see bright red blood, severe pain, vomiting, or can’t keep food down, call us or go to the ER."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2148-07-23 09:05:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. And my heart meds?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2148-07-23 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, all your home medications are continued, including amlodipine, metoprolol, torsemide, and aspirin."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2148-07-23 09:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And follow-up?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2148-07-23 09:07:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll see your surgeon in one to two weeks. We’ll also coordinate home health services to check on you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2148-07-23 09:08:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you so much. I feel like a new person already."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2148-07-23 09:09:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You did great. Take it easy, follow the instructions, and you’ll keep improving."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 61,
      "time": "2148-07-23 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Just a quick check before discharge. Any pain now?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 62,
      "time": "2148-07-23 10:00:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Just a little sore, but manageable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 63,
      "time": "2148-07-23 10:01:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good. And you’re walking independently?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 64,
      "time": "2148-07-23 10:01:20",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, no problem."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 65,
      "time": "2148-07-23 10:01:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Excellent. You’re cleared to go home with services."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 66,
      "time": "2148-07-23 10:02:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m so grateful. Thank you for taking care of me."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 67,
      "time": "2148-07-23 10:02:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re very welcome. Take care and call if anything comes up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 68,
      "time": "2148-07-23 11:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Nurse will go over your discharge instructions one more time, including medications and warning signs."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 69,
      "time": "2148-07-23 11:00:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I’ll listen carefully."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 70,
      "time": "2148-07-23 12:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "One last thing — your labs show mild anemia and low platelets, but that’s consistent with your history. No action needed now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 71,
      "time": "2148-07-23 12:00:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I understand. I’ll follow up with my PCP."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 72,
      "time": "2148-07-23 13:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing really well. Discharge is confirmed for this afternoon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 73,
      "time": "2148-07-23 13:00:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m ready to go home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 74,
      "time": "2148-07-23 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Just signing final orders. Home health will call you tonight."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 75,
      "time": "2148-07-23 14:00:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you again, Doctor."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 76,
      "time": "2148-07-23 14:01:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Have a safe trip home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 77,
      "time": "2148-07-23 14:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Final check — all set for discharge."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 78,
      "time": "2148-07-23 14:30:20",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m so relieved."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 79,
      "time": "2148-07-23 15:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Take these written instructions with you. Call us with any concerns."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 80,
      "time": "2148-07-23 15:00:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thank you for everything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 81,
      "time": "2148-07-23 15:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re discharged. Have a good recovery."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 82,
      "time": "2148-07-23 15:30:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, Doctor. I feel hopeful."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 83,
      "time": "2148-07-23 15:31:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s the best outcome. Take care."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 84,
      "time": "2148-07-23 15:55:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Just confirming — you’re leaving now?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 85,
      "time": "2148-07-23 15:55:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, the transport is here. Goodbye!"
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2148-07-16 13:15:00",
    "admission_end": "2148-07-23 15:57:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A 68-year-old woman was admitted for worsening rectal prolapse with associated fecal incontinence, rectal bleeding, and recent weight gain. She underwent a perineal rectosigmoidectomy with levatorplasty the following day. Post-operatively, she developed a transient post-operative ileus with abdominal distension, managed conservatively without a nasogastric tube. She had low urine output initially, which resolved with IV fluids and restart of home diuretics. A urinalysis before discharge revealed a urinary tract infection, and she was started on ciprofloxacin. Her diet was advanced as bowel function returned, and she passed a bowel movement on hospital day 6. She recovered well, with stable chronic diastolic heart failure and no surgical complications. She was discharged home with services on day 8 with instructions for bowel management, activity restrictions, and follow-up.",
    "problems": [
      "Rectal prolapse",
      "Chronic diastolic heart failure",
      "Congestive heart failure, unspecified",
      "Paralytic ileus",
      "Other digestive system complications",
      "Urinary tract infection, site not specified",
      "Surgical operation with anastomosis, bypass, or graft, with natural or artificial tissues used as implant causing abnormal patient reaction, or later complication, without mention of misadventure at time of operation",
      "Pain in joint, shoulder region",
      "Chest pain, unspecified",
      "Coronary atherosclerosis of native coronary artery",
      "Percutaneous transluminal coronary angioplasty status",
      "Personal history of malignant neoplasm of breast",
      "Unspecified essential hypertension"
    ]
  }
}
